Attribution

The design in this repository is informed by published research, and those
papers are cited by identifier in the documentation. They are not vendored code
and no endorsement is claimed or implied; the attribution here is to record
where the design came from, which is the practice the license asks for and
which the authors consider the honest thing to do.

  - "Governance Decay" (arXiv:2606.22528) -- compaction-induced policy violation
    as a function of constraint survival. Supplies the pinned-buffer design
    (docs/architecture.md section 7) and the stratification of constraint kinds.

  - "Compaction Cliff" (arXiv:2608.22752, CIKM 2026) -- safety-rule survival
    across repeated production /compact operations, and Knowledge Triage as a
    mitigation. Supplies the triage-before-compaction pipeline order
    (docs/architecture.md section 4).

  - "Context Rot" (Chroma research, research.trychroma.com/context-rot) --
    continuous degradation of long-context use, invisible to NIAH. Supplies the
    argument for treating the compaction trigger as a quality decision rather
    than a capacity one.

If any of the constants quoted in the documentation are wrong, the citation is
the fastest way to find the error, and the documentation is expected to be
corrected rather than the claim quietly adjusted.
